IMPORT prelude

-- Revised Edition of the Laws Act 1983 (Singapore) -- who the Law Revision Commissioners are (s 3), what they may change without
-- Parliament (ss 4, 6, 15(2)), what happens to omitted Acts and old instruments (ss 4(1)(a) proviso, 5, 13, 16, 19), what must go
-- into the revised edition (s 8(1)), when a later edition may be published and what its cover says (ss 9, 10, 11(2)), who makes an
-- edition the sole proper law and whether it goes to Parliament (ss 7, 11, 17), print against electronic versions (s 17A), and the
-- rectification of errors (s 23).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RELA1983.txt. The cover says
-- it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the body is annotated with later amendments up to Act 5 of
-- 2025 (in force 9 March 2025), and Act 32 of 2024 (in force 25 November 2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 7 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules with decision content. Not
-- encoded: the definitions (s 2) beyond their use here, the booklet binding rules (s 9(2), (3)), the lists of titles (s 12), the
-- complementary reprints (s 18), the construction of references (s 20) and expenses (s 24). Ss 11A, 21 and 22 are repealed and
-- s 17(6) is deleted in the deposit; their former content was not available and is not guessed at.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Revised Edition of the Laws Act 1983 -- revision`

§§ `3 -- the Law Revision Commissioners`

-- s 3(1): the President may appoint a Law Revision Commission comprising "(a) the Attorney-General; (b) a Deputy Attorney-General;
-- (c) the Solicitor-General; (d) the Chief Legislative Counsel; and (e) any other persons whom the President may appoint".
-- (2): every Commissioner appointed under (1)(e) "holds office for a period not exceeding 3 years" and is eligible for
-- re-appointment. (3): the President may at any time revoke the appointment of any Commissioner appointed under (1)(e).
-- The Act states no term and no revocation power for (a) to (d); this encoding reads that as "no limit stated" (an inference).
DECLARE Office IS ONE OF
    `the Attorney-General`
    `a Deputy Attorney-General`
    `the Solicitor-General`
    `the Chief Legislative Counsel`
    `another person appointed by the President`

GIVEN `the office` IS A Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner is a presidential appointee under paragraph (e)` IF
    CONSIDER `the office`
    WHEN `another person appointed by the President` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the office` IS A Office, `term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term of appointment is within section 3(2)` IF
        (NOT `the Commissioner is a presidential appointee under paragraph (e)` `the office`)
    OR  `term in years` AT MOST 3

GIVEN `the office` IS A Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may revoke the appointment at any time under section 3(3)` IF
    `the Commissioner is a presidential appointee under paragraph (e)` `the office`

-- s 3(5): where a Commissioner is unable to discharge the commission "and no appointment has been made under subsection (4)", the
-- remaining Commissioner or Commissioners "have and may exercise all the powers and duties".
GIVEN `a Commissioner is unable to act` IS A BOOLEAN, `a substitute was appointed under section 3(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the remaining Commissioners may exercise all the powers` IF
    `a Commissioner is unable to act` AND (NOT `a substitute was appointed under section 3(4)`)

§§ `4, 6 and 15(2) -- what the Commissioners may change themselves`

-- s 4(1): the Commissioners have power, "without changing the meaning of any Act", to (a) omit repealed, expired or spent Acts, all
-- Supply Acts, preambles, enacting clauses, commencement provisions and embodied amending Acts; (c) add or alter a long or short
-- title; (f) consolidate Acts in pari materia; (i) renumber; (j)(ii) change "the way of referring to or expressing a number ...
-- amount of money ... penalty"; (j)(iii) change language that indicates gender; (m) correct grammatical and typographical
-- mistakes; (o) correct or update cross-references; (r) restyle Ordinances as Acts.
-- s 6(1): omissions, amendments or additions "other than those authorised by section 4" may be collected and submitted to
-- Parliament "in the form of one or more Acts".
-- s 15(2): for subsidiary legislation the Commissioners have the like powers, but (a) s 6 (other than s 6(2)) is inapplicable and
-- (b) unauthorised amendments are prepared and submitted "for approval to the authority having power to make the same".
-- Changing a penalty's AMOUNT and creating a new offence are not in the list; (j)(ii) reaches only the way a penalty is expressed.
DECLARE Change IS ONE OF
    `omitting a repealed Act`
    `omitting a Supply Act`
    `omitting a preamble`
    `omitting an enacting clause`
    `altering a short title`
    `consolidating Acts in pari materia`
    `renumbering sections`
    `rewriting a penalty in a different form of words`
    `making language gender-neutral`
    `correcting a typographical mistake`
    `updating a cross-reference`
    `restyling an Ordinance as an Act`
    `increasing a penalty`
    `creating a new offence`

GIVEN `the change` IS A Change
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change is of a kind listed in section 4(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the change`
    WHEN `increasing a penalty` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `creating a new offence` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the change` IS A Change, `the change alters the meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioners may make the change under section 4` IF
    `the change is of a kind listed in section 4(1)` `the change` AND (NOT `the change alters the meaning`)

DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `by the Commissioners themselves`
    `only by an Act of Parliament under section 6`
    `only with approval of the authority that makes the subsidiary legislation`

GIVEN `the change` IS A Change, `the change alters the meaning` IS A BOOLEAN, `the text is subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Route
`how the change can be made` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioners may make the change under section 4` `the change` `the change alters the meaning`
    THEN `by the Commissioners themselves`
    ELSE `the route for an unauthorised change` `the text is subsidiary legislation`

GIVEN `the text is subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Route
`the route for an unauthorised change` MEANS
    IF `the text is subsidiary legislation`
    THEN `only with approval of the authority that makes the subsidiary legislation`
    ELSE `only by an Act of Parliament under section 6`

§§ `4(1)(a) proviso, 5, 13 -- omitted Acts`

-- s 4(1)(a) proviso: "section 16 of the Interpretation Act 1965 applies to such omissions in the same manner as if the enactments
-- omitted had been repealed".
-- s 5(2): Acts the President specifies for omission "remain in force until they have been expressly repealed or have expired or
-- become spent or had effect".
-- s 13: an Act omitted, "other than any Act omitted under section 4", is not to be deemed without force "by reason only of the fact
-- that it is so omitted".
DECLARE OmissionGround IS ONE OF
    `omitted by the Commissioners under section 4(1)(a)`
    `omitted on the President's notification under section 5`
    `omitted for some other reason`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A OmissionGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the omission is treated as a repeal` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `omitted by the Commissioners under section 4(1)(a)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A OmissionGround, `expressly repealed, expired, spent or had effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the omitted Act remains in force` IF
        (NOT `the omission is treated as a repeal` `the ground`)
    AND (NOT `expressly repealed, expired, spent or had effect`)

§§ `16 and 19 -- old subsidiary legislation and instruments`

-- s 19(2): instruments made under an Act repealed or omitted for the revision, "so far as they are not inconsistent with any Act for
-- the time being in force, continue in force until otherwise provided".
-- s 16: subsidiary legislation "not revised by the Commissioners remains in force until it has been expressly revoked or has
-- expired, become spent or had effect".
GIVEN `inconsistent with an Act in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `otherwise provided for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an instrument under a repealed or omitted Act continues in force` IF
    (NOT `inconsistent with an Act in force`) AND (NOT `otherwise provided for`)

GIVEN `expressly revoked, expired, spent or had effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unrevised subsidiary legislation remains in force` IF
    NOT `expressly revoked, expired, spent or had effect`

§§ `8(1) -- what the revised edition of Acts must contain`

-- s 8(1): "Subject to sections 4, 5 and 6", the revised edition must include (a) the Constitution; (b) "all Acts wholly or
-- substantially in force on 31 December 2020, and any other Acts coming wholly or substantially into force after that date that
-- the Commissioners think fit to include". s 5(1): the Commissioners "must omit" Acts the President specifies by notification.
-- Acts not in force on 31 December 2020 and not later brought into force fall to the s 4 power to omit (an inference: s 8 is
-- silent on them).
DECLARE Inclusion IS ONE OF
    `must be included`
    `may be included`
    `must be omitted`
    `may be omitted`

GIVEN `the President specified it for omission` IS A BOOLEAN, `in force on 31 December 2020` IS A BOOLEAN, `came into force after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Inclusion
`whether the Act goes into the revised edition` MEANS
    IF `the President specified it for omission`
    THEN `must be omitted`
    ELSE `inclusion apart from section 5` `in force on 31 December 2020` `came into force after that date`

GIVEN `in force on 31 December 2020` IS A BOOLEAN, `came into force after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Inclusion
`inclusion apart from section 5` MEANS
    IF `in force on 31 December 2020`
    THEN `must be included`
    ELSE `inclusion of a later or dead Act` `came into force after that date`

GIVEN `came into force after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Inclusion
`inclusion of a later or dead Act` MEANS
    IF `came into force after that date`
    THEN `may be included`
    ELSE `may be omitted`

§§ `9, 10, 11(2) -- later editions and their covers`

-- s 10(1): the Commissioners may publish (a) a revised edition of any Act "that they consider has been extensively amended"; (b) a
-- revised edition of any new Act, "other than an Act the sole or substantial effect of which was to amend other Acts". (2): "a new
-- revised edition of any Act ... which has not been amended".
-- On this text an existing Act that HAS been amended, but not in the Commissioners' view extensively, is reached by neither (1)(a)
-- nor (2). That is a reading of the words, not a stated rule.
GIVEN `a new Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `its sole or substantial effect is to amend other Acts` IS A BOOLEAN, `has been amended` IS A BOOLEAN, `considered extensively amended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioners may publish a revised edition under section 10` IF
    IF `a new Act`
    THEN NOT `its sole or substantial effect is to amend other Acts`
    ELSE (NOT `has been amended`) OR `considered extensively amended`

-- s 9(1)(a): the front page must carry "The Statutes of the Republic of Singapore" and "2020 Revised Edition". s 11(2): an edition
-- published under s 10 carries the same description "except that for the reference to the 2020 Revised Edition there must be
-- substituted a reference to the year in which the edition is published".
GIVEN `published under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN, `year of publication` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year on the front page` MEANS
    IF `published under section 10` THEN `year of publication` ELSE 2020

§§ `7, 11, 17 -- making an edition the sole proper law`

-- s 7(2), (4): the President by order in the Gazette fixes the date from which the revised edition of Acts is "the sole and only
-- proper Statute Book"; (3) it must be "published and presented to Parliament". s 11(3), (4): the same for an edition under s 10.
-- s 17(2)-(4): the same for a revised edition of subsidiary legislation under s 15. s 17(8): for an edition under s 17(5), the date
-- is fixed "by notification in the Gazette" by THE COMMISSIONERS. The deposit shows no duty to present a s 17(5) edition to
-- Parliament; s 17(6) is marked deleted.
DECLARE Edition IS ONE OF
    `the revised edition of Acts`
    `a later edition of an Act under section 10`
    `a revised edition of subsidiary legislation under section 15`
    `a revised edition of subsidiary legislation under section 17(5)`

DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `the President, by order in the Gazette`
    `the Commissioners, by notification in the Gazette`

GIVEN `the edition` IS A Edition
GIVETH A Authority
`who fixes the date it becomes the sole proper law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the edition`
    WHEN `a revised edition of subsidiary legislation under section 17(5)` THEN `the Commissioners, by notification in the Gazette`
    OTHERWISE `the President, by order in the Gazette`

GIVEN `the edition` IS A Edition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the edition must be presented to Parliament` IF
    CONSIDER `the edition`
    WHEN `a revised edition of subsidiary legislation under section 17(5)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `17A -- print and electronic versions`

-- s 17A(1): an electronic revised edition is "prima facie evidence of the proper law". (2): "To the extent of any inconsistency",
-- an electronic version published on or after the appointed date prevails over "the same revised edition published in print"
-- on or after that date. (3): a print version published before the appointed date prevails over the electronic version published
-- before that date. (4): the appointed date is the commencement of s 3(m) of the Electronic Gazette and Legislation Act 2025 (that
-- date is not in the deposit).
-- Where the print and electronic versions fall on opposite sides of the appointed date, s 17A says nothing.
DECLARE Prevailing IS ONE OF
    `the electronic version`
    `the print version`
    `section 17A does not say`

GIVEN `electronic published on or after the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN, `print published on or after the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Prevailing
`which version prevails on an inconsistency` MEANS
    IF `electronic published on or after the appointed date` AND `print published on or after the appointed date`
    THEN `the electronic version`
    ELSE `prevailing where not both after` `electronic published on or after the appointed date` `print published on or after the appointed date`

GIVEN `electronic after` IS A BOOLEAN, `print after` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Prevailing
`prevailing where not both after` MEANS
    IF (NOT `electronic after`) AND (NOT `print after`)
    THEN `the print version`
    ELSE `section 17A does not say`

§§ `23 -- rectification of errors`

-- s 23(1): the Commissioners may by order in the Gazette rectify "any clerical or publication error" in (a) the revised edition of
-- Acts or an edition under s 10, or (b) a revised edition of subsidiary legislation, "or rectify in a manner not inconsistent with
-- the powers of revision conferred by this Act any other error so appearing". (2): "Every order made under section (1)(a) must be
-- presented to Parliament" -- so an order correcting subsidiary legislation under (1)(b) need not be. ("section (1)(a)" is as
-- printed; it is read as subsection (1)(a).)
GIVEN `a clerical or publication error` IS A BOOLEAN, `rectification is consistent with the revision powers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioners may rectify the error` IF
    `a clerical or publication error` OR `rectification is consistent with the revision powers`

GIVEN `the error is in an edition of Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rectification order must be presented to Parliament` IF
    `the error is in an edition of Acts`
